<div class="mb-requirement-container">
  <div class="mb-requirement-item">
    <div class="mb-requirement-parent mb-requirement-id-16277">
      <span class="mb-requirement-listnumber"> </span>
      <b>NOTE: </b> Check out the Digital Resource Guide for the Competitive
      Gaming merit badge
      <a
        href="https://www.scouting.org/skills/merit-badges/digital-resource-guides/competitive-gaming/"
        target="_blank"
        >HERE</a
      >
      for detailed information and helpful resources to engage your learning and
      assist you along on your merit badge journey!
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="mb-requirement-item">
    <div class="mb-requirement-parent mb-requirement-id-16278">
      <span class="mb-requirement-listnumber"> 1. </span>
      <b>History of Gaming.</b> Do the following:
    </div>
    <ul class="mb-requirement-children-list">
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16278 mb-requirement-id-16279">
        (a) Create a timeline showing how video gaming has evolved since 1958.
        Include at least one significant event from each decade. <br /><i
          >Resources:</i
        >
        <a
          href="https://www.museumofplay.org/video-game-history-timeline/"
          target="_blank"
          >Video Game History Timeline (website)</a
        ><br />
        <a href="https://youtu.be/vQ0XSceaPNs" target="_blank"
          >The History of Video Games: From Pong to Fortnite (video)</a
        ><br />
        <a
          href="https://www.pbs.org/kcts/videogamerevolution/history/index.html"
          target="_blank"
          >The Video Game Revolution (website)</a
        ><br />
        <a
          href="https://www.si.edu/sidedoor/ep-15-worst-video-game-ever?page=1"
          target="_blank"
          >The Worst Video Game Ever (website w/ video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16278 mb-requirement-id-16280">
        (b) Identify and define five major video game genres. Provide an example
        for each. <br /><i>Resources:</i>
        <a href="https://glitchwave.com/games/genre/" target="_blank"
          >Glitchwave Game Genres (website)</a
        ><br />
        <a
          href="https://esportsinsider.com/esports-genres-explained"
          target="_blank"
          >Esports Genres Explained (website)</a
        ><br />
        <a
          href="https://gamedesigning.org/gaming/video-game-genres/"
          target="_blank"
          >Explore All Video Game Genres (website)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16278 mb-requirement-id-16281">
        (c) Explain the difference between video gaming and esports. Include how
        esports incorporates elements of organized competition such as teams,
        tournaments, rules, coaching, and spectatorship. Provide two examples of
        games that are commonly played casually as video games but are also used
        in organized esports competition. <br /><i>Resources:</i>
        <a
          href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/12HVwGZbzfuvZNJ1fT7Htygk7BgyFnSXF/view"
          target="_blank"
          >Gaming vs. Esports (video)</a
        ><br />
        <a
          href="https://hwb.gov.wales/keeping-safe-online/views-from-the-experts/video-gaming-and-esports-the-differences-and-distinctions-in-detail"
          target="_blank"
          >Video Gaming and Esports (website)</a
        ><br />
        <a
          href="https://help.playvs.com/en/articles/5915810-game-title-overview"
          target="_blank"
          >PlayVS Game Title Overview (website)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16278 mb-requirement-id-16282">
        (d) Identify and define five major moments in the development of esports
        as an industry since 1990. Include key tournaments, technological
        advances, and organizations that helped shape competitive gaming
        globally. Discuss your findings with your counselor. <br /><i
          >Resource:</i
        >
        <a
          href="https://whatisesports.xyz/major-milestones-esports-history-timeline/"
          target="_blank"
          >Major Milestones in Esports History: A Timeline (website)</a
        >
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div style="padding-left: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: #515354"></div>
    <br />
  </div>
  <div class="mb-requirement-item">
    <div class="mb-requirement-parent mb-requirement-id-16283">
      <span class="mb-requirement-listnumber"> 2. </span>
      <b>Living the Scout Oath and Law Online.</b> Do the following:
      <b><br />Note:</b> View the Personal Safety Awareness "Digital Safety"
      video (with your parent or guardian's permission.) <br /><i>Resource:</i>
      <a
        href="https://filestore.scouting.org/filestore/YPSAT/YT%20Mod1%20Final%20Master%20Small.mp4"
        target="_blank"
        >Digital Safety (video)</a
      >
    </div>
    <ul class="mb-requirement-children-list">
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16283 mb-requirement-id-16284">
        (a) Define the term "toxicity in gaming." Describe a real or
        hypothetical example of toxic behavior in online play and outline how
        the situation could be prevented or resolved by applying the Scout Oath
        and Law. <br /><i>Resources:</i>
        <a
          href="https://staticctf.ubisoft.com/8aefmxkxpxwl/1wJowtd0nH3HS8gAANwF3i/0d0f9fe2d3f9ac6315e069b109aad640/Good_Game_Playbook_for_Teens_EN.pdf"
          target="_blank"
          >Good Game Playbook for Teens (PDF)</a
        ><br />
        <a
          href="https://alltogethernow.org.au/our-work/far-right-extremism/game-changers-resources-guide/"
          target="_blank"
          >Game Changer Resource Guide (website)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16283 mb-requirement-id-16285">
        (b) List five strategies for handling negative online gaming
        experiences. Describe how each strategy reflects a point of the Scout
        Oath or Law. <br /><i>Resources:</i>
        <a
          href="https://www.twoaveragegamers.com/how-to-deal-with-toxic-players-a-gamers-guide-to-staying-sane-online/"
          target="_blank"
          >How To Deal With Toxic Players: A Gamer's Guide to Staying Sane
          Online (website)</a
        ><br />
        <a
          href="https://www.childline.org.uk/info-advice/bullying-abuse-safety/types-bullying/bullying-cyberbullying/"
          target="_blank"
          >Bullying and Cyberbullying (website)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16283 mb-requirement-id-16286">
        (c) Research the Entertainment Software Rating Board (ESRB) rating
        system. Record the ratings of the video games you own and compare them
        to your age group. Explain to your counselor whether you agree with the
        ESRB descriptions. <br /><i>Resources:</i>
        <a
          href="https://www.internetmatters.org/resources/video-games-age-ratings-explained/"
          target="_blank"
          >Video Games Age Ratings Explained (website)</a
        ><br />
        <a href="https://www.esrb.org/search/" target="_blank"
          >Search ESRB Game Ratings (website)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16283 mb-requirement-id-16287">
        (d) List five ways to create a positive online gaming environment for
        yourself and others. Demonstrate one of these methods with your troop,
        patrol, or family. <br /><i>Resources:</i>
        <a
          href="https://www.twoaveragegamers.com/the-ultimate-guide-to-non-toxic-gaming-communities/"
          target="_blank"
          >The Ultimate Guide to Non-Toxic Gaming Communities (website)</a
        ><br />
        <a
          href="https://www.stopbullying.gov/kids/what-you-can-do"
          target="_blank"
          >What Kids Can Do (website)</a
        >
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div style="padding-left: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: #515354"></div>
    <br />
  </div>
  <div class="mb-requirement-item">
    <div class="mb-requirement-parent mb-requirement-id-16288">
      <span class="mb-requirement-listnumber"> 3. </span>
      <b>Gamer Health and Balance.</b> Do the following:
    </div>
    <ul class="mb-requirement-children-list">
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16288 mb-requirement-id-16289">
        (a) Read two credible articles describing positive aspects of video
        gaming and two describing negative aspects. Create a chart showing where
        the articles agree or disagree. <br /><i>Resources:</i>
        <a
          href="https://www.popsci.com/health/video-game-benefits/"
          target="_blank"
          >The Surprising Benefits of Video Games (website)</a
        ><br />
        <a
          href="https://health.clevelandclinic.org/are-video-games-good-for-you"
          target="_blank"
          >Are Video Games Good for You? (website)</a
        ><br />
        <a
          href="https://www.ted.com/talks/kris_alexander_how_video_games_can_level_up_the_way_you_learn"
          target="_blank"
          >How Video Games Can Level Up the Way You Learn (video)</a
        ><br />
        <a
          href="https://www.kidsvillepeds.com/blog/1290873-how-video-games-affect-kids-behavioral-health-the-hidden-risks/"
          target="_blank"
          >How Video Games Affect Kids' Behavioral Health: The Hidden Risks
          (website)</a
        ><br />
        <a
          href="https://www.brightpathbh.com/effects-of-video-games-on-teen-mental-health/"
          target="_blank"
          >Effects of Video Games on Teen Mental Health (website)</a
        ><br />
        <a
          href="https://www.sciencejournalforkids.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/screentime-ADHD_Article.pdf"
          target="_blank"
          >What Is the Link Between Screen Time and ADHD? (PDF)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16288 mb-requirement-id-16290">
        (b) Track the amount of gaming you do each day for two weeks. Record and
        summarize your results. <br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a href="https://activitywatch.net/" target="_blank"
          >ActivityWatch (website)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16288 mb-requirement-id-16291">
        (c) Track your daily physical activity for the same two weeks. Compare
        your results to the CDC recommendation of one hour of
        moderate-to-vigorous activity per day for youth ages 6-17. <br /><i
          >Resource:</i
        >
        <a
          href="https://www.cdc.gov/healthyweight/pdf/physical_activity_diary_cdc.pdf"
          target="_blank"
          >My Physical Activity Diary (website)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16288 mb-requirement-id-16292">
        (d) Track your daily sleep for the same two weeks. Compare your results
        to the CDC recommendation of 9-12 hours for ages 6-12 and 8-10 hours for
        ages 13-18. <br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a
          href="https://thesleepcharity.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/The-Sleep-Charity-Teens-Sleep-Diary.pdf"
          target="_blank"
          >Teen Sleep Diary (PDF)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16288 mb-requirement-id-16293">
        (e) After completing 3(b), 3(c), and 3(d), create a one-week balanced
        schedule that includes healthy sleep, physical activity, and agreed-upon
        gaming time. Follow this schedule and summarize your results. <br /><i
          >Resource:</i
        >
        <a
          href="https://www.cci.health.wa.gov.au/~/media/CCI/Mental-Health-Professionals/Depression/Depression-Worksheets/Depression-Worksheet---03---Weekly-Activity-Schedule.pdf"
          target="_blank"
          >Weekly Activity Schedule (website)</a
        >
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div style="padding-left: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: #515354"></div>
    <br />
  </div>
  <div class="mb-requirement-item">
    <div class="mb-requirement-parent mb-requirement-id-16294">
      <span class="mb-requirement-listnumber"> 4. </span>
      <b>Gamer Safety and Community Connection. </b>Do the following:
    </div>
    <ul class="mb-requirement-children-list">
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16294 mb-requirement-id-16295">
        (a) Explain the benefits and risks of gaming online. <br /><i
          >Resources:</i
        >
        <a
          href="https://builtin.com/articles/online-gaming-social-benefits"
          target="_blank"
          >The Real Benefits of Video Games (website)</a
        ><br />
        <a
          href="https://www.smartsocial.com/post/negative-effects-video-games"
          target="_blank"
          >Negative Effects of Video Games (website)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16294 mb-requirement-id-16296">
        (b) Research and list ten ways to stay safe when playing video games
        online. <br /><i>Resources:</i>
        <a href="https://www.internetmatters.org/issues/" target="_blank"
          >Online Safety Issues (website)</a
        ><br />
        <a
          href="https://www.dhs.gov/sites/default/files/2024-09/24_09_20_K2P_Gaming-Safety.pdf"
          target="_blank"
          >Gaming Safety (PDF)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16294 mb-requirement-id-16297">
        (c) Play one of your favorite games with your parent or guardian for at
        least 30 minutes. Demonstrate how to use privacy and safety settings,
        explain what you enjoy about the game, and let them play for part of the
        session. <br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a
          href="https://internetsafety101.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Gaming-controls-quick-guide-03-24-2025.pdf"
          target="_blank"
          >Online Gaming Safety Settings (PDF)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16294 mb-requirement-id-16298">
        (d) Play an online or local multiplayer game with another Scout, friend,
        or community member in a cooperative or team-based setting. The match
        may be casual or competitive. During play, demonstrate positive
        communication, teamwork, and sportsmanship. Afterward, review the
        experience with your counselor and describe how cooperation and
        communication influenced your team's performance and overall enjoyment
        of the game.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div style="padding-left: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: #515354"></div>
    <br />
  </div>
  <div class="mb-requirement-item">
    <div class="mb-requirement-parent mb-requirement-id-16299">
      <span class="mb-requirement-listnumber"> 5. </span>
      <b>Technology in Competitive Gaming.</b> Do the following:
    </div>
    <ul class="mb-requirement-children-list">
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16299 mb-requirement-id-16300">
        (a) Explain the difference between console gaming and PC gaming. List
        the advantages and disadvantages of each. <br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a
          href="https://www.seagate.com/blog/console-vs-pc-gaming/"
          target="_blank"
          >Console vs. PC Gaming: Which Is Better? (website)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16299 mb-requirement-id-16301">
        (b) Play the same game on at least two different platforms. Describe the
        similarities and differences in gameplay and performance. <br /><b
          >Note:</b
        >
        Any game may be used, including free games, on any platform (phone,
        tablet, PC, laptop, console, etc.).
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16299 mb-requirement-id-16302">
        (c) Visit a PC builder website such as PCPartPicker or Micro Center.
        Design your ideal gaming PC and create a parts list that includes:
        central processing unit (CPU), motherboard, random access memory (RAM),
        hard drive, power supply, graphics card, fans, case. Discuss your
        selections with your counselor. <br /><i>Resources:</i>
        <a href="https://pcpartpicker.com/" target="_blank"
          >PCPartPicker (website)</a
        ><br />
        <a
          href="https://www.microcenter.com/site/content/custom-pc-builder.aspx?k=1772572403500"
          target="_blank"
          >Micro Center (website)</a
        >
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div style="padding-left: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: #515354"></div>
    <br />
  </div>
  <div class="mb-requirement-item">
    <div class="mb-requirement-parent mb-requirement-id-16303">
      <span class="mb-requirement-listnumber"> 6. </span>
      <b>Leadership and Service in Competitive Gaming. </b>Do ONE of the
      following:
    </div>
    <ul class="mb-requirement-children-list">
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16303 mb-requirement-id-16304">
        (a) Teach your troop, patrol, or a group of younger Scouts or family
        members about online gaming safety or digital citizenship.
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16303 mb-requirement-id-16305">
        (b) Attend or view a live-streamed esports event online, such as a
        professional tournament, collegiate match, or school-level competition.
        Take notes on how the broadcast team presents the event, how players
        communicate, and how the audience interacts digitally. Share with your
        counselor what you learned about the structure and presentation of
        online esports competition.
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16303 mb-requirement-id-16306">
        (c) Attend an esports tournament, convention, or community event that
        includes a competitive gaming activity or demonstration. Attend with
        another Scout, troop member, or family member. Afterward, share with
        your counselor what you learned about the atmosphere of live esports
        events and how the experience changed your understanding of playing
        games competitively in front of an audience.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div style="padding-left: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: #515354"></div>
    <br />
  </div>
  <div class="mb-requirement-item">
    <div class="mb-requirement-parent mb-requirement-id-16307">
      <span class="mb-requirement-listnumber"> 7. </span>
      <b>Exploring Professions in the Competitive Gaming Industry. </b>Do the
      following:
    </div>
    <ul class="mb-requirement-children-list">
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16307 mb-requirement-id-16308">
        (a) Research two colleges that offer varsity esports programs. Record
        the following information for each: availability and amount of gaming
        scholarships, offered gaming or IT-related degrees, games played by the
        esports team, league or association in which the team competes. <br /><i
          >Resource:</i
        >
        <a href="https://www.nacesports.org/school-directory" target="_blank"
          >NACE School Directory (website)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16307 mb-requirement-id-16309">
        (b) Research three gaming-adjacent careers that support or connect to
        the esports industry but are not esports athlete roles. Examples may
        include: game designer or developer, shoutcaster or broadcast producer,
        data analyst or statistician, marketing or event coordinator, IT or
        network support specialist. For each career, identify the main
        responsibilities, education or training requirements, and how the role
        contributes to the success of the gaming or esports ecosystem. <br /><i
          >Resources:</i
        >
        <a
          href="https://www.flipbookpdf.net/web/site/0f69cbe0b3ab4127778010bc84c0383f86c1f5a5FBP25582848.pdf.html#page/5"
          target="_blank"
          >100 Jobs in Esports (website)</a
        ><br />
        <a href="https://hitmarker.net/" target="_blank">Hitmarker (website)</a>
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16307 mb-requirement-id-16310">
        (c) Visit the "Careers" or "Jobs" page of a major game publisher (such
        as Blizzard, Riot, Epic or Nintendo). Choose three jobs that interest
        you. For each, identify the required education, skills, and experience.
        <br /><i>Resources:</i>
        <a href="https://careers.blizzard.com/global/en" target="_blank"
          >Careers at Blizzard Entertainment (website)</a
        ><br />
        <a href="https://www.riotgames.com/en/work-with-us" target="_blank"
          >Riot Games - Work With Us (website)</a
        ><br />
        <a href="https://www.epicgames.com/site/en-US/careers" target="_blank"
          >Epic Games Careers, Jobs and Employment Opportunity (website)</a
        ><br />
        <a href="https://careers.nintendo.com/" target="_blank"
          >Careers at Nintendo of America (website)</a
        >
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div style="padding-left: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: #515354"></div>
    <br />
  </div>
</div>
